.TH "RTCERROR.SCTPCAUSECODE" "3JS" "August 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
RTCError.sctpCauseCode \- RTCError: sctpCauseCode property
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]sctpCauseCode\f[B]\f[R] read\-only property of the
\f[CR]RTCError\f[R] interface provides the SCTP cause code explaining
why the SCTP negotiation failed, if the \f[CR]RTCError\f[R] represents
an SCTP error.
.SH VALUE
A positive integer specifying the SCTP cause code explaining why the
error occurred.
This property must only be set if \f[CR]errorDetail\f[R] is
\f[CR]sctp\-failure\f[R], and is otherwise \f[CR]null\f[R].
.PP
The standard SCTP error cause codes, numbered 1\-13, are defined in the
SCTP specification: RFC 4960, section 3.3.10.
